Decided: drive reads a remote reviewer's verdict.md live when the pass's batched look had none (rev idle, exited, or pickup failed) and records it via `drover verdict` if it names the PR head.
Because: "A boat reviewer's finished `verdict.md` is recorded within one drive pass, whether the reviewer ran `drover verdict` (via the outbox) or only wrote the file."
Because: crates/core/src/snapshot.rs:163 a remote read the look's batch lost is cached as None for the whole pass, with its ssh error dropped, so the scan saw a finished review as "reviewer exited without a verdict" and re-reviewed it.
Decided: a failed fetch or failed `drover verdict` logs a passive `verdict-pickup-failed` with its reason (deduped per review), holds the re-review, and waiting shows it until a pass works.
Because: "A failed pickup (ssh error, file missing) is logged with its reason and retried next pass, never left as 'recording within 1 min'."
Decided: a missing verdict.md (cat's "No such file") keeps today's path: an exited reviewer is reviewed again.
Rejected: copying the remote file to the state dir and recording that copy — no_proof, repro and verify shots read --file on the lane's host, so a local copy would break them.
Rejected: one more live read inside the scan — the scan also feeds the board and status, which must never ssh on a request path.
